{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/6525","createdAt":"2026-10-04T17:20:00Z","decision":"accept_intent","decisionDigest":"sha256:c716e24c7011776e8f6bd129de5389220a0a990322801190409a2ffbf5035814","decisionId":"rdec-14e17b87941b1b74710c4867ab990875","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:78f1a218d51d4047310c5a7c645a77b7bc397dddb91c5e90f2401fe1f970ee41","packageIdentity":"epkg-f39bbfe65ac9747b9210608999e3d7849e924a02541c9794fbc590046801d8ea","prNumber":"6525","reason":"Agree with the intent, with one regression to fix first: inline // comments now parse, but a whole-line comment indented with a non-ASCII space now empties the whole menu file. At head 913e112d, a trailing // comment after content parses (1 row, where quattro c05d9019 drops the file), // inside a string survives, trailing commas still parse, and menu-test.sh passes (130 ok). The regression: a no-break space, U+2028, U+3000, a vertical tab or a form feed indenting a // line, or a BOM later in the file, makes the file contribute 0 rows, because JSON.parse accepts only ASCII whitespace. Copying any such character outside a string as a plain space keeps the old behaviour. #13968 fixes the same inline-comment bug (#13493), so whichever lands second needs a rebase.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
